Preamble

This license is not a suggestion. It is a binding, enforceable, copyleft agreement that governs any use, distribution, modification, sublicensing, or commercial exploitation of the software, system, architecture, documentation, and derivative works known as NexusBox and all associated modules (Nexus Ads Engine, Nexus Compression, Nexus Disk Forensic, Nexus AI Compression, Nexus OS Inspector, and any future contribution made by the original author).

By downloading, cloning, forking, installing, executing, or integrating any part of this software, you accept the full terms of this license. If you do not accept, you must delete all copies immediately and refrain from any use.

This license is designed to be viral, dominant, and irreversible. It forces every downstream user, including enterprises, cloud providers, AI laboratories, and competitors, to contribute back to the ecosystem. Any attempt to circumvent it is a violation of copyright law and will be prosecuted.

---

Article 1 — Definitions

1.1 "Software" means the source code, binary code, documentation, architecture, schemas, scripts, datasets, and any related material distributed under this license.

1.2 "Author" means Aïssa Mohammedi, also known as DGK, sole creator and copyright holder.

1.3 "You" means any individual, company, foundation, state entity, AI laboratory, cloud provider, or automated system that uses the Software.

1.4 "Derivative Work" means any modification, extension, integration, translation, recompilation, reverse engineering, or recombination of the Software, in any language or form.

1.5 "Commercial Use" means any use of the Software by an entity generating revenue, directly or indirectly, including SaaS, PaaS, IaaS, embedded systems, and AI training pipelines.

1.6 "Gain" means any revenue, profit, funding, grant, investment, or financial benefit obtained through the Software or any Derivative Work.

---

Article 2 — Grant of Rights

Subject to full compliance with this license, the Author grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, revocable right to:

a) Use the Software for personal, educational, or research purposes.
b) Modify the Software and produce Derivative Works.
c) Distribute the Software and Derivative Works, provided that the full terms of this license are preserved and applied to any downstream recipient.

No other rights are granted. All rights not explicitly granted are reserved by the Author.

---

Article 3 — Copyleft Obligation

3.1 Any Derivative Work, in any language, must be released under this exact same license (NEXUS-OPEN-DOMINANT v1.0) without modification of its terms.

3.2 Any distribution of the Software or a Derivative Work must include the full license text, the copyright notice, and a direct link to the original repository.

3.3 Any entity integrating the Software into a larger system must ensure that this license extends to the entire system, unless a written exemption is granted by the Author.

---

Article 4 — Gain Sharing Clause

4.1 Any individual or entity that obtains any Gain through the Software or a Derivative Work must share 15% (fifteen percent) of the net Gain with the Author, calculated on a quarterly basis.

4.2 The 15% applies to:

· Direct sales of the Software or Derivative Works
· SaaS subscriptions based on the Software
· Funding raised specifically for a project using the Software
· Revenue from AI training pipelines using the Software
· Licensing fees received by a third party using the Software

4.3 Payment must be made within 30 days following the end of each fiscal quarter, with a detailed report of the Gain calculation.

4.4 Failure to report or pay constitutes a material breach of this license and will result in immediate termination of rights and legal action.

4.5 Any entity that publicly credits the Author in their product or website may be eligible for a reduced rate of 10%, upon written approval.

---

Article 5 — Attribution Requirement
5.
1 Every copy, distribution, or public display of the Software must include:

· The full name of the Author: Aïssa Mohammedi (DGK)
· A direct link to the original repository
· The exact text: "Powered by NexusBox — NEXUS-OPEN-DOMINANT License"

5.2 Any product, service, or system using the Software must display this attribution in a visible location: about page, footer, documentation, or equivalent.

5.3 Removing or obscuring the attribution is a violation of this license.

---

Article 6 — Forced Contribution Back

6.1 Any improvement, optimization, module, or feature added to the Software must be contributed back to the original repository within 90 days of the first use in production.

6.2 The contribution must be made through a public pull request or an equivalent method, under this same license.

6.3 The Author reserves the right to accept or reject any contribution.

6.4 Rejected contributions may be reused by the contributor in their own fork, provided the fork also complies with this license.

---

Article 7 — Prohibited Uses

You may not:

a) Re-license the Software under any license other than this one.
b) Sell the Software as a closed-source product.
c) Remove or modify the copyright notices.
d) Use the Software to train AI models without contributing 15% of the Gain from those models.
e) Claim authorship of the Software or any Derivative Work.
f) Use the name "NexusBox" or "DGK" without written permission.
g) Circumvent the Gain sharing clause through shell companies, proxies, or jurisdictional tricks.
h) Distribute a modified version under a different name to hide the origin.

---

Article 8 — Viral Extension to Cloud Providers

8.1 Any cloud provider (AWS, Google Cloud, Microsoft Azure, OVH, Scaleway, Hetzner, or any other) that offers the Software as a service must:

· Disclose the use publicly
· Pay the 15% Gain share for revenue generated from the Software
· Include the attribution in their service description

8.2 Any AI laboratory (OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepMind, Meta AI, Mistral, or any other) that uses the Software for training, inference, or orchestration must:

· Contribute 15% of any funding raised for projects involving the Software
· Contribute 15% of any revenue derived from those projects
· Publish a public statement of use

8.3 Any enterprise with over 1,000 employees must file a yearly compliance report with the Author, detailing the use of the Software.

---

Article 9 — Enforcement

9.1 Any violation of this license results in:

· Immediate termination of all rights
· Legal action under the copyright laws of France, the European Union, and any jurisdiction where the violation occurs
· Recovery of unpaid Gain shares, plus a penalty of 50% of the amount owed
· Injunction to cease all use

9.2 The Author reserves the right to assign enforcement to a third party, including a legal firm, an open-source foundation, or an automated system.

9.3 Public disclosure of violators is permitted and encouraged, without any liability on the Author's part.

9.4 The Author will pursue any violation, regardless of the size of the entity, including multinational corporations, sovereign funds, and government agencies.

